{"path": "frontier/sources/i79_logarithmic_girth_spectra_novelty_r3/outside/preprints/The-mean-analytic-rank-of-quadratic-twists-of-elliptic-curves-October-6-2026/paper.pdf.txt", "sha256": "432d15b668d599fb9a881d90a307c3afac25476e4401e0a4be26577d095664fc", "count": 1, "excerpts": [[10782, " of Lemma 4.1, forced by the vanishing of a derivative\nof order k of the completed L-function. Its Dirichlet-series weight is obtained by exponentially\nsmoothing a k-th power of a truncated logarithm. Near the square root of the conductor, at\nlengths of order X for twists of height X, this weight suppresses the late terms. The approximation\n(1 \u2212 u)k \u2248 e\u2212ku for u = O(1/k) motivates mollification: at u = log n/ log X, the exponential\ncorresponds to a small positive shift from the center of "]]}
{"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-26/new-discoveries/lanes/pi-euler-turan-final-review/fresh/trureturing/D5/S1/Recurrence/Interpolation/CullinanYoungKrawtchouk.lean", "sha256": "9e6b82e3b4f1d0c35c806ab172391367931d9108fab926284568df2af5de38c2", "count": 8, "excerpts": [[39, "/- GID: D5/S1/Recurrence/Interpolation/CullinanYoungKrawtchouk\n   generality: G\n   mirror-B: D5/B/S1/Recurrence/Interpolation/CullinanYoungKrawtchouk\n   mirror-E: none(waiver:external-open-problem-resolution)\n   anchors: []\n   utility: none\n   digest: Cullinan\u2013Young\u2019s even Krawtchouk sign interpolant coefficient formula is proved. -/\n\n/- Pub"], [126, "/- GID: D5/S1/Recurrence/Interpolation/CullinanYoungKrawtchouk\n   generality: G\n   mirror-B: D5/B/S1/Recurrence/Interpolation/CullinanYoungKrawtchouk\n   mirror-E: none(waiver:external-open-problem-resolution)\n   anchors: []\n   utility: none\n   digest: Cullinan\u2013Young\u2019s even Krawtchouk sign interpolant coefficient formula is proved. -/\n\n/- Public source proposition: claim.\n   The claim retains the literal source sum and product,"], [252, "lity: G\n   mirror-B: D5/B/S1/Recurrence/Interpolation/CullinanYoungKrawtchouk\n   mirror-E: none(waiver:external-open-problem-resolution)\n   anchors: []\n   utility: none\n   digest: Cullinan\u2013Young\u2019s even Krawtchouk sign interpolant coefficient formula is proved. -/\n\n/- Public source proposition: claim.\n   The claim retains the literal source sum and product, without duplicate definitions;\n   private interpolate_source identifies them with Mathlib Lagrange.interpolate for the proof."], [2278, "a.BigOperators.Field\nimport Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Intervals\nimport Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination\n\nset_option autoImplicit false\n\nnamespace D5.S1.Recurrence.Interpolation.CullinanYoungKrawtchouk\n\nopen Polynomial\n\nnoncomputable def ell (N i : \u2115) : \u211a[X] :=\n  \u220f j \u2208 (Finset.range (N + 1)).erase i,\n    C (1 / ((i : \u211a) - j)) * (X - C ((j : \u211a) - (N : \u211a) / 2))\n\nnoncomputable def I (N : \u2115) : \u211a[X] :=\n  \u2211 i \u2208 Finset.range (N + 1),\n    C ((SignType.sign ((i : \u211a) "], [2637, " - (N : \u211a) / 2))\n\nnoncomputable def I (N : \u2115) : \u211a[X] :=\n  \u2211 i \u2208 Finset.range (N + 1),\n    C ((SignType.sign ((i : \u211a) - (N : \u211a) / 2) : SignType) : \u211a) * ell N i\n\n/-- Cullinan\u2013Young, arXiv:2603.05408, Remark 8: \"Numerical experimentation suggests that the\nleading coefficient of I_N(x) (and, therefore, F_N(x)) is given by (\u22121)^{(N\u22122)/2} C((N\u22122)/2)/(N\u22121)!,\nwhere C(n) is the nth Catalan number\" (for even `N`). -/\ndef claim : Prop :=\n  \u2200 N : \u2115, 2 \u2264 N \u2192 Even"], [3094, "  \u2200 N : \u2115, 2 \u2264 N \u2192 Even N \u2192\n    (I N).leadingCoeff = (-1) ^ ((N - 2) / 2) * (catalan ((N - 2) / 2) : \u211a) / ((N - 1).factorial : \u211a)\n\nend D5.S1.Recurrence.Interpolation.CullinanYoungKrawtchouk\n\nnamespace D5.S1.Recurrence.Interpolation.CullinanYoungKrawtchouk\nopen Polynomial Finset\n\nprivate lemma interpolate_source (N : \u2115) :\n    (Lagrange.interpolate (Finset.range (N+1)) (fun j : \u2115 => (j : \u211a) - (N : \u211a)/2) (fun i : \u2115 => (SignType.sign ((i : \u211a) - (N : \u211a)/2) : \ufffd"], [3160, ") ^ ((N - 2) / 2) * (catalan ((N - 2) / 2) : \u211a) / ((N - 1).factorial : \u211a)\n\nend D5.S1.Recurrence.Interpolation.CullinanYoungKrawtchouk\n\nnamespace D5.S1.Recurrence.Interpolation.CullinanYoungKrawtchouk\nopen Polynomial Finset\n\nprivate lemma interpolate_source (N : \u2115) :\n    (Lagrange.interpolate (Finset.range (N+1)) (fun j : \u2115 => (j : \u211a) - (N : \u211a)/2) (fun i : \u2115 => (SignType.sign ((i : \u211a) - (N : \u211a)/2) : \u211a))) =\n      I N := by\n  simp only [I, ell, Lagrange.interpolate_a"], [17266, " 0)\n  have hNeq : N = 2*(m+1) := by omega\n  rw [hNeq, show (2*(m+1)-2)/2 = m by omega, show 2*(m+1)-1 = 2*m+1 by omega]\n  exact leading_even m\n\n\nend D5.S1.Recurrence.Interpolation.CullinanYoungKrawtchouk\n"]]}
{"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-26/new-discoveries/lanes/pi-euler-turan-final-review/fresh/trureturing/D5/S3/Arith/Lacunary/LacunarySequence.lean", "sha256": "1c88d0097f834321915ca5ca5a7419bff1f68f0d7b226d04c98753a202c89b6f", "count": 1, "excerpts": [[1487, "ength of an initial segment bounded by `x` is at most the nonnegative\npart of the logarithmic bound. The maximum handles the empty segment, for which\n`x` is unrestricted and the untruncated logarithmic bound can be negative. -/\ntheorem card_lt_of_lacunary {a : \u2115 \u2192 \u211d} {c : \u211d} (h : IsLacunary a c) (x : \u211d) (N : \u2115)\n    (hmem : \u2200 n < N, a n \u2264 x) : (N : \u211d) \u2264 max 0 (Real.logb c (x / a 0) + 1) := by\n  have hc : 0 < c := lt_trans zero_lt_one h.1\n  have ha : 0 < a 0 := h.2.1 0\n  cases"]]}
